  "scientific_review": [
    "Eleven regional scenarios across ten current identities, using31 existing source reference anchors. No new observations or canonical depth references.343 qualified depth references and both regional core-volume scenarios remain unchanged; physical whole-route profiles and whole-current volumes remain zero.",
    "Northward EICC case uses a single February–April seasonal mean of the Sen2022 repeating-climatology ROMS product. Simulation lasted eight years, analyzing the last three, without mapping those years to forcing or validation calendar dates. It is not three independent monthly depth records or a whole-year seasonal cycle.",
    "At source sectionC12N, the reported core-location band0–100m is retained as a nominal support interval; no50m midpoint is invented. At sectionA19.3N, approximately150m is retained as a nominal degenerate support descriptor, which does not mean zero physical uncertainty.",
    "At intervening sectionB16N, the source specifically describes northward flow as approximately20m deep and surface-confined. The projected0–20m core-support interval is conditional on the local maximum lying within that described layer. It is not a reported core band, direct core measurement, guaranteed physical bound or statistical interval. Generic reported reach, especially an inclusive minimum reach, does not authorize this inference.",
    "The B constraint breaks interpolation. Directly connecting the C and A descriptors across B would miss the described shallow layer. Lower/upper nominal support limits instead interpolate separately between adjacent C/B/A sections in latitude; intervening source constraints cannot be dropped to obtain a smoother profile.",
    "Interpolated display limits round outward to10m and retain unrounded computations separately. No scalar midpoint, interval-width thickness, confidence interval, physical upper/lower boundary, annual extrema, longitudinal axis or OSW route distance is supplied. Values outside12–19.3N remain unknown.",
    "New comparison data preserve native source metrics for both northward February–April and southward October–December means at the named sections. Northward B remains a reach descriptor in the native table rather than a falsely reported core point. Missing southward A core remains unknown; the region-wide200m southward reach is not assigned to it. No automatic numeric core-depth shift or monthly interpolation is performed across incompatible native quantities.",
    "All previous ten profile records and all prior CSV quantity cells are preserved. New interval columns and conditional-support kinds are explicit; scalar depth fields for new interval samples stay empty. The November reference-route drawing is not reused as northward phase geometry.",
    "Eighty cloud checks include seven current source tests,65 preceding profile tests and eight new interval/phase tests. Six baseline checks also pass:86 total. New checks verify mandatory intervening support, band and point meanings, outward rounding without midpoint, unsupported latitude gaps, invalid interval/order rejection, phase/model/metric mutation, comparison-table unknowns and typed CSV reproduction.",
    "Only small metadata generation used one idle local CPU; no new raw ocean-field processing. All tests ran in cloud. No runtime/WASM/browser/server execution, physical-state allocation, volume admission or UI/playback integration."
  ],
  "source_review_scope": "Primary publisher indexed full text for Sen et al.doi:10.1080/1755876X.2020.1846266, Section3.3, rechecked for section coordinates, phase averaging, A/C maximum-velocity descriptors and B approximate surface confinement. Direct full-page open returned403; no original Figure11 pixels or digitization claimed. Source access https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/1755876X.2020.1846266.",
